# 🌐 LLMNR / Responder-Based Credential Capture

## 📌 Overview
LLMNR poisoning exploits fallback name resolution to capture authentication attempts.

---

## 🎯 Objective
Capture NTLM authentication attempts in a controlled environment.

---

## 🧭 Workflow (High-Level)

1. Monitor network traffic
2. Identify broadcast name resolution requests
3. Observe authentication attempts
4. Capture credential artifacts (lab only)

---

## 🔍 What to Look For

### 📡 Network Indicators
- LLMNR broadcasts
- NetBIOS name queries

---

### 🔐 Credential Artifacts
- NTLMv2 challenge-response
- Username + domain

---

### ⚠️ Risk Indicators
- Users accessing unknown shares
- Repeated failed lookups

---

## 🛡️ Detection

- Monitor multicast traffic
- SIEM alerts for abnormal authentication
- IDS/IPS signatures

---

## 🔐 Prevention

- Disable LLMNR
- Disable NetBIOS
- Enforce SMB signing

---

## 🧠 DPCI Notes

- Treat captured hashes as sensitive evidence
- Record timestamps + source machine
- Preserve logs for court use
